    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0467" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/53</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Chase to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-27T18:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 27, 1917—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This morning Minister of War Tinoco overcame the Government of President González
                    by force having taken possession of all arms; some dead; streets quiet; martial
                    law. Berliner, Department of Justice, aiding; Consul and all American civilians
                    apparently in no danger.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
